# --- secrets ---
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# --- node ---
node_modules/
dist/
backend/public/
build/
coverage/
*.tsbuildinfo
.turbo/

# --- dev harness (standards.md §3-§7) ---
# Quality-gate reports, the reviewer's JSONL log, dispatched worktrees, the
# leader's plan files and the per-agent env override. Plans MUST stay ignored:
# an untracked plan in the shared parent tree dirties `git status` and blocks
# every other leader's dispatch at the parent-clean gate.
.quality-gate/
.claude/worktrees/
.claude/plans/
.claude/settings.local.json
.agent-env
*.log

# --- python (legacy) ---
__pycache__
*.pyc

# --- media: never commit audio ---
# The corpus pipeline downloads ~170 MB of audio per sermon into its work
# directory (default /mnt/Data/ipp-sermons-work, see tools/corpus-update).
# Nothing but .txt transcripts and metadata.csv is meant to enter the repo.
*.wav
*.mp3
*.opus
*.m4a
*.aac
*.ogg
*.webm
*.flac
*.gz
work/

# --- rendered artifacts (standards.md §8, ratified 2026-07-21) ---
# Validators, Playwright probes and UI reviewers are SUPPOSED to render these;
# they must never enter git. Denied by location rather than by filename prefix,
# because every new agent invents a new filename and prefix lists always lose.
# The deny stays total; source images get a scoped exception below, never a
# dropped rule.
*.png
*.jpg
*.jpeg
*.gif
*.webp
*.pdf
# The one scoped exception: README screenshots, curated by hand.
!docs/images/*.png
**/screenshots/
**/.playwright-mcp/
test-results/

# Rendered HTML is an artifact at the repo root and under docs/. It is real
# SOURCE under frontend/ (the Vite entry point) — never blanket-ignore *.html.
/*.html
docs/**/*.html

# --- notebooks carrying live credentials ---
# archive/notebooks/metadata.ipynb hardcodes a Spotify client_id/client_secret
# pair in its cells. The file is kept on disk because it documents the original
# scraping pipeline, but it must not be tracked. Untracking only stops FUTURE
# exposure: the pair is already reachable from published history (9bec37b
# onward), so rotating the credential is the actual fix, not this line.
archive/notebooks/metadata.ipynb

# Experiment output from `pnpm compare:topics`. The decision it informs gets
# committed; the raw comparison does not.
.compare/
